// Your Former Life (D10), p.24-25. "Disease Resistance" (Healer) and "Quick Feet" (Outcast) don't exist, so they're dropped (Patrick, 2026-10-12). Noble's Diplomacy and Leadership are PRE Skills (the book says WIL).
(
    name: "Former Occupation",
    die: D10,
    entries: [
        (1, 1, (title: "Peasant Farmer/Serf", text: "You know the rhythms of the earth, how to read the seasons, and how to coax life from stubborn soil. You are no stranger to back-breaking labor, hunger, and loss.", skills: [HeavyLifting, Hardy, Insight], trouble: "You are used to being overlooked and powerless. You carry a deep-seated resentment for the nobility and clergy who failed you.")),
        (2, 2, (title: "Clergy (Monk, Priest, Nun)", text: "You were a keeper of faith, literate and learned in scripture. You saw the Choir's arrival from the inside, witnessing the holy ecstasy curdle into madness.", skills: [Theology, Investigation, InnerStrength], trouble: "You are haunted by the failure of your faith and may be a target for both Penitents who see you as a rival and Unmade who see you as a symbol of the sky-borne plague.")),
        (3, 3, (title: "Craftsman", text: "You are a creator. A blacksmith, weaver, mason, or carpenter. You know how to turn raw materials into things of use and value. Your hands know work that is precise and meaningful.", skills: [BruteForce, NimbleFingers, Haggling], trouble: "You see the world in terms of things that can be fixed and built, a view that is constantly challenged by a world being unmade.")),
        (4, 4, (title: "Soldier", text: "You lived by the sword, either in a lord's service or for coin. You know the grim reality of combat, the weight of armor, and the fear in a man's eyes before he dies.", skills: [BattleFrenzy, PrecisionStrikes, MentalFortitude], trouble: "You are trained to follow orders in a world where leaders are insane or dead. Violence is your only tool, and you see every problem as a fight to be won.")),
        (5, 5, (title: "Noble", text: "You were born to rule. You understand power, lineage, and the art of commanding others. You have seen the world from the top, and you remember it.", skills: [Tactics, Diplomacy, Leadership], trouble: "Your name is now meaningless, your lands are gone, and your authority is a ghost. You are haunted by the weight of your lost responsibility and the faces of the people you failed to protect.")),
        (6, 6, (title: "Trader", text: "Your world was one of roads, coins, and contracts. You know the value of things and how to read the desires of people. You are a natural negotiator and traveler.", skills: [EndlessStamina, Haggling, Networking], trouble: "Your wealth is worthless and the roads are death traps. You see everyone as a potential customer or a rival, a transactional view that isolates you from true connection.")),
        (7, 7, (title: "Hunter", text: "You lived on the fringes, in the wild places. You know how to move unseen, to track prey, and to survive on what the land provides.", skills: [Ambusher, Stealth, Naturalism], trouble: "You are unused to people and distrustful of settlements. The horrors of the apocalypse are just a new, more aggressive form of predator in your world.")),
        (8, 8, (title: "Scholar", text: "You were a creature of ink and parchment, a keeper of knowledge. You may have been a university student, a monastic scribe, or a court academic.", skills: [LoreMastery, PuzzleSolving, SelfReflection], trouble: "Most of your knowledge is now useless or dangerous. You are physically ill-suited for survival and prone to seeking answers in books while the world burns around you.")),
        (9, 9, (title: "Healer", text: "You understand the secrets of the body, of herbs and poultices that can mend wounds and cure sickness. You have seen the fragility of life up close.", skills: [Healing, MindOverMatter], trouble: "Your craft is now seen as witchcraft by the desperate. You are faced with wounds and plagues that no poultice can fix, and the Choir's \"miracles\" mock your humble art.")),
        (10, 10, (title: "Outcast (Beggar, Leper, Excommunicate, etc.)", text: "You were already at the bottom. Society had cast you out, and you survived on scraps and pity. You had nothing to lose when the world ended.", skills: [Hardy, LipReading], trouble: "You trust no one and expect the worst from everyone. You have survived, but you have no memory of a better world to give you hope or strength.")),
    ],
)
